<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Walter Burley Griffin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1876">1876</a>–<a href="/years/1937">1937</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Walter Burley Griffin was an American architect of the Prairie School who, with his wife <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marion-mahony-griffin">Marion Mahony Griffin</a>, won the international competition of 1912 to design <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>'s new capital, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canberra">Canberra</a>. He directed the city's early construction until 1920, though his plan was only partly realised, centred on the lake later named after him. He later worked in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sydney-nova-scotia">Sydney</a> and died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lucknow">Lucknow</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/walter-burley-griffin.jpg" alt="Walter Burley Griffin" width="320" height="404" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Walter_Burley_Griffin_1912.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The plan for Canberra came from an international competition won in 1912 by the American architect <b>Walter Burley Griffin</b>, with drawings by his wife and partner Marion Mahony Griffin.</blockquote><a href="/empire/commonwealth-of-australia">Commonwealth of Australia · At a glance</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Maywood, in what is now <a href="/countries/united-states">the United States</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lucknow">Lucknow</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/india">India</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=41.88,-87.84&amp;year=1915" aria-label="Maywood on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2413 672 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Walter Burley Griffin"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2863 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M2863 942h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=41.88,-87.84&amp;year=1915">What was here in 1915? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
